# Checksums for everything scripts/toolchain installs, in `sha256sum -c`
# format so the verification is the standard tool and not a string compare of
# our own.
#
# ⚠️ TAKEN FROM EACH PROJECT'S OWN PUBLISHED CHECKSUM, not from a download:
# the Go project's download index, jq's published checksum file and OpenTofu's
# SHA256SUMS, all read on 2026-09-09. A checksum computed from the file you just fetched proves
# only that the file downloaded intact, which is not the question.
#
# ⚠️ BOTH ARCHITECTURES, because this repository ships both: release.yml
# builds truss-linux-arm64 beside truss-linux-amd64 and the Dockerfile is
# parameterised by TARGETARCH. A checksum file that covered only the machine
# it was written on would make the installer refuse on half of them.
#
# ⚠️ scripts/toolchain refuses if this file and its own version table
# disagree about which files exist. Two statements of one fact drift; the
# repository has paid for that three times.
